SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Checkmate" with Ben Mezrich
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot left\nSta
 tus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /187622\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into the high-stak
 es world of Checkmate with bestselling author Ben Mezrich—an electrifyin
 g true story that unravels the biggest scandal in modern chess.\n\nIn Sept
 ember 2022\, the chess world was shaken when nineteen-year-old American pr
 odigy Hans Niemann defeated reigning world champion Magnus Carlsen in a st
 unning upset. Days later\, Carlsen accused Niemann of cheating—an allega
 tion that ignited a global firestorm\, drawing in Chess.com\, the media\, 
 and a rapidly expanding digital audience. What followed was a dramatic col
 lision of reputation\, rivalry\, and power.\n\nBut Checkmate is about far 
 more than controversy. It’s a portrait of ambition at its sharpest edge�
 ��a young player willing to risk everything to rise\, and a legendary figu
 re determined to defend his legacy. Set against the backdrop of a centurie
 s-old game transformed by streaming\, sponsorships\, and Silicon Valley in
 fluence\, Mezrich brings readers inside a world that is as cutthroat as it
  is cerebral.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622
CATEGORIES:The Arts
